# Who must review a change before it can merge to main (security audit M3,
# 27 Oct 2026; paths widened after the 4 Nov 2026 assessment). The workflows
# hold real credentials: db-backup.yml has the full database password,
# eas-update.yml the Expo token. A change to them, or to anything that runs in
# those jobs or in every agent session, needs the owner's review, so a bad
# merge can't quietly send a credential somewhere else.
#
# This file only takes effect with branch protection on main:
# Settings -> Branches -> main -> "Require a pull request before merging" ->
# "Require review from Code Owners" (ACCOUNTS_BETA_PLAN.md section 9 and its
# go-live gates). On a PRIVATE repository that needs GitHub Pro; on the Free
# plan this file is ignored. If a workflow ever changes without that review,
# rotate the database password (docs/mobile/SCALING.md, runbooks).
